//
// EVERY FORM'S SHAPE IS CHECKED AT ITS DEFINITION (`@FR-Op-Shape`, with `@FR-Op-Def`).  `compare`
// takes `self` and one more and answers `Ordering`; the arithmetic forms take `self` and one more;
// `negate` and `next` take `self` alone, `next` answering the item or null; `to_text` takes `self`,
// or `self` and `spec: text`, and answers `text`.  Each definition below breaks one of those on a
// type of its own, and each is refused where it is written with the shape the form wants — no
// use of any form is needed.  Op-Def's cell holds a wrong `compare` answer and a first parameter
// that is not `self`; these are the arities and the `to_text` and `next` shapes.
//
// Axes it MOVES: the form (`plus`, `remainder`, `negate`, `next`, `to_text`, `compare`), the fault
//   (an operand missing, one too many, a spec of the wrong type, an answer of the wrong type).
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator plus` takes `self` and the right operand of `+`, and answers the result
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator remainder` takes `self` and the right operand of `%`, and answers the result
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator negate` takes `self` alone and answers the result of `-x`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator next` has the wrong shape: `operator next(self: T) -> E?`, answering null when the walk is done
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator compare` takes `self` and the value it is compared with, and answers an `Ordering`
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator to_text` has the wrong shape
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator to_text` has the wrong shape
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator to_text` has the wrong shape
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; every refusal fired as expected, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostics.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: each diagnostic names the shape its form wants.
// HOLDS: every definition of the right shape compiles (Op-Back's every-form cell).

struct S1 { x: integer }
struct S2 { x: integer }
struct S3 { x: integer }
struct S4 { x: integer }
struct S5 { x: integer }
struct S6 { x: integer }
struct S7 { x: integer }
struct S8 { x: integer }

// An operand missing, and one too many.
operator plus(self: S1) -> S1 { self }
operator remainder(self: S2, a: S2, b: S2) -> S2 { a }
// `self` alone, given more.
operator negate(self: S3, o: S3) -> S3 { o }
operator next(self: S4, k: integer) -> integer? { k }
// `compare` with nothing to compare with.
operator compare(self: S5) -> Ordering { Equal }
// `to_text`: a spec that is not text, an answer that is not text, a third parameter.
operator to_text(self: S6, spec: integer) -> text { "s6" }
operator to_text(self: S7) -> integer { 7 }
operator to_text(self: S8, spec: text, extra: text) -> text { "s8" }

fn test_the_definitions_are_refused() {
  s = S1 { x: 1 };
  assert(s.x == 1, "unreachable");
}
